I agree about the enshittification risk, and it will happen like for many other fields: search, browsers, ads, games, web, TVs, esp. when it will be the only viable way of squeezing more profits from models which will stop progressing so fast.
It was recently teased by Mr. Amodei: &quot;some tokens Claude outputs are worth a few cents. Others could be worth tens of millions of dollars.&quot;
In this example the idea is to charge your more per token (or in quota) when they will classify your prompt and output as more valuable.
